Review PR #543 in this repository (kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec).

Steps:
1. Get the PR diff: gh pr diff 543
2. Get PR details: gh pr view 543 --json title,body,files
3. Check the PR body for Task: trailer — this is task @task-e2e-daemon-tasks-api (no spec_ref, infrastructure task). AC coverage checks are N/A since there is no spec. Focus on code quality.
4. Review the code for:
   - Correctness: do the tests actually verify the behaviors they claim?
   - Test completeness: are edge cases covered? Are any important scenarios missing?
   - Test quality: no fluff tests that always pass regardless of implementation
   - Test isolation: each test must use the daemon fixture (not share state improperly)
   - Code style: consistent with other E2E test files in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/
   - Potential state pollution: some tests mutate task state (start, note). Do later tests in the same suite see mutated state?
   - Playwright request API usage: is it correct? Are request bodies passed correctly?
   - Error handling test coverage: 404, 400, 409 all covered?
5. Write a review to /tmp/codex-pr-543-review.md with MUST-FIX, SHOULD-FIX, SUGGESTION items
6. Post to GitHub:
   Write JSON to /tmp/codex-pr-review-body.json:
   {"event":"COMMENT","body":"summary","comments":[{"path":"file","line":N,"body":"comment"}]}
   Then post: gh api repos/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pulls/543/reviews --method POST --input /tmp/codex-pr-review-body.json
   
   IMPORTANT: Use event "COMMENT" not "REQUEST_CHANGES" — this repo prohibits requesting changes on your own PR.

Work from the project root: /workspace
Do not start any background services or long-running processes.
