MUST-FIX

- "'`packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:337` and `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:360` assert the wrong response shape for `POST /api/tasks/:ref/note`. The route currently returns `{ success, note, task }` (see `packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts`), but the tests expect a top-level task object with `notes`. As written, these tests do not verify the implemented contract and will fail if executed.
- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:103` (comma-separated status filter) can pass even when the feature is broken because it never asserts that any tasks were returned. The current server implementation does not split comma-separated status values, so this test currently passes vacuously on an empty `items` array while claiming AC coverage for comma support.
- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:271` weakens the `/start` “full task shape” test by accepting `409` based on a shared-state assumption. The `daemon` fixture in `packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/test-base.ts` is test-scoped (no worker scope is configured), so each test starts from a fresh fixture. Accepting `409` here can mask a regression where `start` is broken for pending tasks.
- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:377` expects `400 { error: '"'validation_error' }"'` for missing note content, but the route declares `body: t.Object({ content: t.String() })` in `packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts`. That schema can reject the request before the custom handler-level validation runs, so this test is likely asserting the wrong status/shape for the actual daemon behavior.

SHOULD-FIX

- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:66` makes the `spec_ref` test conditional (`if (taskWithSpecRef)`), which means it passes even if the list endpoint stops returning `spec_ref` entirely. Since the fixtures include tasks with `spec_ref`, this should assert that at least one such task exists and validate it.
- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:221` is named “resolves task by ULID prefix” but sends the full ULID (`@${firstTask._ulid}`) at `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:229`. Either use a unique prefix to test prefix resolution or rename the test to exact ULID resolution.
- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:73` and `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:87` have the same empty-result false-positive risk as the comma-separated filter test. Add a non-empty assertion (or compare to known fixture expectations) before checking statuses.

SUGGESTION

- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:399` says “for all endpoints” but only exercises two GET endpoints. Either rename the test to reflect GET coverage only or include representative POST endpoints (including mutation endpoints) and assert JSON content type on their responses.
- `packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-tasks.spec.ts:22` and the repeated `daemon` parameter in every test are redundant. Existing E2E files usually trigger the fixture per test via the test signature alone; keeping one pattern would reduce noise.
